# DIAGNOSTICS

A stream the receiver refuses ends send with why: `bad arg in system call` for an incremental whose <from> isn't what `recv/`<sys> holds, `file already exists` for a whole snapshot into one that holds another.
fs's `status` says how each receive went (fs(4)).

# BUGS

A stream that fails partway leaves `recv/`<sys> as far as it got, with nodes in `recv/`<sys>`/.receiving`; the same stream sent again finishes it.
A sender's file named `.receiving` at its volume's top would collide with that directory.
Only one volume's streams should go to one <sys>: a second sender's whole snapshot there is refused.
